@startuml
' SPSCRING-DOC-SDD, figure 5-1: the ring's states as its two counters define them (DEC-001: full counters, every slot usable)
title SPSCring: the ring's states (n = tail - head, N = capacity)
hide empty description
[*] --> Empty : spsc_ring_init(N)\nhead = tail = 0
state "Empty\nn == 0" as Empty
state "Partial\n0 < n < N" as Partial
state "Full\nn == N" as Full
Empty --> Partial : push / 0\n(N > 1)
Empty --> Full : push / 0\n(N == 1)
Partial --> Partial : push / 0, pop / 0
Partial --> Full : push / 0\n(n becomes N)
Partial --> Empty : pop / 0\n(n becomes 0)
Full --> Partial : pop / 0\n(N > 1)
Full --> Empty : pop / 0\n(N == 1)
Empty --> Empty : pop / -1\n(nothing taken)
Full --> Full : push / -1\n(nothing stored)
Partial --> Empty : reset\n(both sides stopped)
Full --> Empty : reset\n(both sides stopped)
Empty --> [*] : spsc_ring_destroy
Partial --> [*] : spsc_ring_destroy
Full --> [*] : spsc_ring_destroy
note right of Full
  head and tail only grow (64-bit);
  the slot of index i is buf[i & (N - 1)]
end note
@enduml
